var e={id:`indonesia`,name:`Indonesia`,flag:`🇮🇩`,currency:`IDR`,language:`Indonesian (Bahasa Indonesia)`,greeting:{text:`Selamat datang`,meaning:`Welcome`},bestMonths:[5,6,7,8,9],tips:[`Most visitors need a Visa on Arrival (buy the e-VOA online beforehand to skip the airport queue).`,`Bali charges every foreign visitor a one-off tourist levy of IDR 150,000; pay online via Love Bali before arrival.`,`Use the Grab or Gojek apps for cars, motorbike taxis and food; in Jakarta, the MRT and TransJakarta buses beat the traffic.`,`Wear a sarong and sash at temples (usually lent or rented at the gate) and never point your feet at shrines.`,`Do not drink tap water — use bottled or refill stations — and carry small notes, as change is often scarce.`,`Use your right hand to give, receive and eat; the left hand is considered unclean.`],cities:[{id:`bali`,name:`Bali`,lat:-8.4095,lng:115.1889,timezone:`Asia/Makassar`,tagline:`Island of temples, rice terraces and surf at sunset`,description:`Indonesia's Hindu island combines emerald rice terraces and jungle temples around Ubud with surf beaches, cliff-top sunsets and beach clubs in the south. Distances are short but traffic is slow, so base yourself in two areas rather than day-tripping everywhere.`,idealDays:[5,10],places:[{id:`tegallalang-rice-terraces`,name:`Tegallalang Rice Terraces`,localName:`Ceking Rice Terrace`,category:`nature`,tags:[`iconic`,`rice-terraces`,`photo-spot`,`swing`],area:`Tegallalang`,lat:-8.4312,lng:115.279,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:2,rating:5,description:`Sweeping tiers of rice paddies carved into a palm-fringed valley, irrigated by the ancient subak system.`,tip:`Arrive by 7:30am for soft light and no crowds; small "donation" fees are asked at several paths, so carry small notes.`,indoor:!1},{id:`sacred-monkey-forest`,name:`Sacred Monkey Forest Sanctuary`,localName:`Mandala Suci Wenara Wana`,category:`nature`,tags:[`monkeys`,`temple`,`jungle`,`kids`],area:`Ubud`,lat:-8.5188,lng:115.2586,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:8,rating:4,description:`A mossy jungle sanctuary of banyan trees and moss-covered temples home to over 1,000 long-tailed macaques.`,tip:`Leave sunglasses, hats and snacks in your bag — the monkeys are expert thieves; do not make eye contact.`,indoor:!1},{id:`ubud-palace`,name:`Ubud Palace & Legong Dance`,localName:`Puri Saren Agung`,category:`culture`,tags:[`palace`,`dance`,`performance`,`heritage`],area:`Ubud`,lat:-8.5069,lng:115.2625,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:7,rating:4,description:`The royal palace courtyard is free to explore by day and becomes an open-air stage for traditional Legong and Barong dances at night.`,tip:`Performances start around 7:30pm; buy tickets from vendors outside during the day and arrive early for front seats.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Ubud Palace`},{id:`ubud-art-market`,name:`Ubud Art Market`,localName:`Pasar Seni Ubud`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`market`,`handicrafts`,`bargaining`,`rainy-day`],area:`Ubud`,lat:-8.5073,lng:115.263,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A covered, multi-level market of sarongs, rattan bags, wood carvings and paintings opposite Ubud Palace.`,tip:`Bargain hard — opening prices are often double; mornings get the best "first sale" prices.`,indoor:!0},{id:`campuhan-ridge-walk`,name:`Campuhan Ridge Walk`,category:`nature`,tags:[`hiking`,`free`,`sunrise`,`walking`],area:`Ubud`,lat:-8.5036,lng:115.2547,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`An easy paved trail along a grassy ridge between two jungle rivers, with views of palms, rice fields and distant volcanoes.`,tip:`Start at the Gunung Lebah temple before 7am to avoid the heat, and continue to Karsa Kafe for breakfast among the paddies.`,indoor:!1},{id:`museum-puri-lukisan`,name:`Museum Puri Lukisan`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`balinese`,`rainy-day`,`gardens`],area:`Ubud`,lat:-8.5063,lng:115.2604,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:6,rating:3,description:`Bali's oldest art museum, tracing traditional and modern Balinese painting and woodcarving in pavilions set around lotus ponds.`,tip:`Ticket includes a drink at the garden café.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Museum Puri Lukisan`},{id:`arma-museum`,name:`ARMA Museum`,localName:`Agung Rai Museum of Art`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`rainy-day`,`gardens`,`workshops`],area:`Ubud`,lat:-8.5199,lng:115.264,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:6,rating:3,description:`A fine private collection of Balinese and Indonesian art, including works by Walter Spies, in lush grounds that also host dance and craft classes.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Agung Rai Museum of Art`},{id:`tirta-empul`,name:`Tirta Empul Temple`,localName:`Pura Tirta Empul`,category:`culture`,tags:[`temple`,`holy-spring`,`purification`,`iconic`],area:`Tampaksiring`,lat:-8.4153,lng:115.3153,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:5,rating:4,description:`A 10th-century water temple where Balinese and visitors bathe under spouts of a sacred spring in ritual purification.`,tip:`Bring a change of clothes; a special sarong is required to enter the pools and is rented on site.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Tirta Empul`},{id:`mount-batur-sunrise`,name:`Mount Batur Sunrise Trek`,localName:`Gunung Batur`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`hiking`,`volcano`,`sunrise`,`guided`],area:`Kintamani`,lat:-8.2421,lng:115.375,durationHours:6,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:45,rating:4,description:`A pre-dawn 2-hour climb up an active volcano to watch sunrise over Lake Batur and Mount Agung, with breakfast cooked on volcanic steam.`,tip:`Hotel pickups start around 2am; bring a warm layer and headlamp — it is cold at the 1,717m summit.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Mount Batur`},{id:`ulun-danu-beratan`,name:`Ulun Danu Beratan Temple`,localName:`Pura Ulun Danu Beratan`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`temple`,`lake`,`highlands`,`photo-spot`,`iconic`],area:`Bedugul`,lat:-8.2752,lng:115.1668,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:5,rating:4,description:`Tiered meru shrines appear to float on misty Lake Beratan in the cool central highlands — the temple on the IDR 50,000 note.`,tip:`Clouds roll in by midday, so go early; pair with Jatiluwih rice terraces on the same day.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Pura Ulun Danu Bratan`},{id:`jatiluwih-rice-terraces`,name:`Jatiluwih Rice Terraces`,category:`nature`,tags:[`unesco`,`rice-terraces`,`walking`,`cycling`],area:`Jatiluwih`,lat:-8.3709,lng:115.1316,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:4,rating:4,description:`UNESCO-listed terraces spanning over 600 hectares beneath Mount Batukaru — vaster and far quieter than Tegallalang.`,tip:`Walk the marked red or blue trails through the paddies; lunch at a warung with valley views.`,indoor:!1},{id:`tanah-lot`,name:`Tanah Lot Temple`,localName:`Pura Tanah Lot`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`temple`,`sea-temple`,`sunset`],area:`Tabanan`,lat:-8.6212,lng:115.0868,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:5,rating:5,description:`A 16th-century sea temple perched on a rock outcrop amid crashing waves, silhouetted dramatically at sunset.`,tip:`At low tide you can walk to the base and receive a blessing from the holy spring; arrive an hour before sunset.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Tanah Lot`},{id:`uluwatu-temple-kecak`,name:`Uluwatu Temple & Kecak Fire Dance`,localName:`Pura Luhur Uluwatu`,category:`culture`,tags:[`iconic`,`temple`,`cliff`,`sunset`,`dance`,`performance`],area:`Uluwatu`,lat:-8.8291,lng:115.0849,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:13,rating:5,description:`A temple on a 70m cliff above the Indian Ocean, where a hypnotic Kecak dance of 70 chanting men is staged against the sunset.`,tip:`Buy Kecak tickets on arrival (it sells out) and secure your sunglasses — the temple monkeys snatch them.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Pura Luhur Uluwatu`},{id:`single-fin`,name:`Single Fin`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`bar`,`surf`,`sunset`,`clifftop`,`live-music`],area:`Uluwatu`,lat:-8.8152,lng:115.088,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:4,description:`A legendary clifftop bar overlooking the Uluwatu surf break, packed for sunset beers and its Sunday-night party.`,tip:`Come at 5pm to watch surfers on the break below; Sunday is the big night.`,indoor:!1},{id:`potato-head-beach-club`,name:`Potato Head Beach Club`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`beach-club`,`sunset`,`pool`,`design`],area:`Seminyak`,lat:-8.6796,lng:115.1529,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:35,rating:4,description:`An iconic beach club with an infinity pool facing the ocean, a façade of reclaimed shutters and DJs into the night.`,tip:`Walk-in entry is free but daybeds require a minimum spend; arrive by 3pm on weekends for a spot.`,indoor:!1},{id:`batu-bolong-beach`,name:`Batu Bolong Beach`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`surf`,`surf-lessons`,`beach`,`sunset`],area:`Canggu`,lat:-8.6594,lng:115.1301,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:3,description:`Canggu's main surf beach, with gentle, beginner-friendly waves, board rentals and surf schools right on the sand.`,tip:`Take a lesson at mid-tide in the morning; stay for sunset beanbags and Bintangs on the beach.`,indoor:!1},{id:`jimbaran-bay-seafood`,name:`Jimbaran Bay Seafood Dinner`,category:`food`,tags:[`seafood`,`beach`,`sunset`,`grill`],area:`Jimbaran`,lat:-8.7785,lng:115.165,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:4,description:`Candlelit tables set right on the sand where cafés grill fresh fish, prawns and clams over coconut husks as the sun sets.`,tip:`Seafood is priced by weight — confirm the price per 100g before they cook it.`,indoor:!1},{id:`waterbom-bali`,name:`Waterbom Bali`,category:`family`,tags:[`waterpark`,`kids`,`slides`],area:`Kuta`,lat:-8.7284,lng:115.1688,durationHours:5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:40,rating:4,description:`One of Asia's top-rated waterparks, with thrilling slides like the Climax drop set in shady tropical gardens.`,tip:`Book online for a discount and go on a weekday; lockers and towels cost extra.`,indoor:!1},{id:`beachwalk-shopping-center`,name:`Beachwalk Shopping Center`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`mall`,`rainy-day`,`air-conditioned`,`sunset`],area:`Kuta`,lat:-8.718,lng:115.169,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`An open-plan, air-conditioned mall across from Kuta Beach with surf brands, a cinema and restaurants overlooking the sea.`,tip:`Grab an upper-level table for sunset over Kuta Beach if the weather turns.`,indoor:!0},{id:`bali-museum`,name:`Bali Museum`,localName:`Museum Bali`,category:`museum`,tags:[`history`,`rainy-day`,`ethnography`,`architecture`],area:`Denpasar`,lat:-8.6572,lng:115.2185,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:4,rating:3,description:`Bali's main ethnographic museum, in palace-style pavilions displaying masks, textiles, ceremonial objects and prehistoric finds.`,tip:`Combine with Puputan Square opposite and the Badung Market a short walk away.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Bali Museum`},{id:`goa-gajah`,name:`Goa Gajah (Elephant Cave)`,category:`culture`,tags:[`temple`,`cave`,`archaeology`,`heritage`],area:`Bedulu`,lat:-8.5233,lng:115.2873,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:3,rating:3,description:`An 11th-century meditation cave entered through the gaping mouth of a carved demon, with ancient bathing pools and a jungle stream below.`,tip:`Sarongs are lent at the entrance; walk down past the pools to the quiet riverside Buddhist ruins.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Goa Gajah`},{id:`gunung-kawi`,name:`Gunung Kawi Temple`,localName:`Pura Gunung Kawi`,category:`culture`,tags:[`temple`,`archaeology`,`rice-terraces`,`heritage`],area:`Tampaksiring`,lat:-8.4237,lng:115.3121,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:3,rating:4,description:`Ten 11th-century royal shrines carved into the cliffs of a lush river gorge, reached by some 300 steps past rice terraces.`,tip:`Combine with Tirta Empul a few minutes away; the climb back up is steep, so go early.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Gunung Kawi`},{id:`taman-ayun`,name:`Taman Ayun Temple`,localName:`Pura Taman Ayun`,category:`culture`,tags:[`temple`,`unesco`,`gardens`,`architecture`],area:`Mengwi`,lat:-8.5418,lng:115.1726,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:5,rating:4,description:`A 17th-century royal temple of the Mengwi kingdom, ringed by a moat and manicured lawns, with elegant tiers of meru shrines.`,tip:`An easy stop on the way to Tanah Lot or the central highlands.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Taman Ayun`},{id:`tirta-gangga`,name:`Tirta Gangga Water Palace`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`water-palace`,`gardens`,`photo-spot`,`day-trip`],area:`Karangasem`,lat:-8.412,lng:115.5873,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:5,rating:4,description:`A former royal water palace of ornamental pools, fountains and stepping stones across ponds of giant koi, set against green hills in east Bali.`,tip:`Arrive by 8am to have the stepping stones to yourself, and pair it with Lempuyang Temple.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Tirta Gangga`},{id:`lempuyang-temple`,name:`Lempuyang Temple (Gates of Heaven)`,localName:`Pura Lempuyang Luhur`,category:`culture`,tags:[`temple`,`photo-spot`,`sunrise`,`mount-agung`,`day-trip`],area:`Karangasem`,lat:-8.3914,lng:115.6296,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:6,rating:4,description:`A hillside temple whose split gate frames Mount Agung in one of Bali's most photographed views; the full pilgrimage climbs about 1,700 steps to the highest shrine.`,tip:`Arrive around sunrise — the queue for the gate photo can exceed two hours later in the day, and the "reflection" is a mirror trick by local photographers.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Pura Lempuyang Luhur`},{id:`besakih-temple`,name:`Besakih Mother Temple`,localName:`Pura Besakih`,category:`culture`,tags:[`temple`,`mount-agung`,`iconic`,`heritage`],area:`Besakih`,lat:-8.3741,lng:115.451,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:10,rating:4,description:`Bali's holiest temple complex, a sprawl of more than 80 shrines terraced up the slopes of sacred Mount Agung.`,tip:`The ticket includes a shuttle up from the car park; ignore touts insisting a private guide is compulsory.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Besakih`},{id:`nusa-penida-day-trip`,name:`Nusa Penida (Kelingking Beach)`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`island`,`day-trip`,`cliffs`,`snorkelling`,`photo-spot`,`manta-rays`],area:`Nusa Penida`,lat:-8.7505,lng:115.4745,durationHours:9,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:60,rating:4,description:`A rugged island about 45 minutes by fast boat from Sanur, famed for the T-Rex-shaped cliffs of Kelingking Beach and snorkelling with manta rays.`,tip:`Roads are rough and slow — pick a tour of either the west or the east coast, not both in one day.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Nusa Penida`},{id:`tegenungan-waterfall`,name:`Tegenungan Waterfall`,localName:`Air Terjun Tegenungan`,category:`nature`,tags:[`waterfall`,`swimming`,`photo-spot`],area:`Gianyar`,lat:-8.5751,lng:115.2893,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:2,rating:3,description:`A broad, thundering waterfall in a jungle gorge just south of Ubud, with a swimming area at its base and plenty of steps to climb.`,tip:`Visit early before the tour buses; swimming is not allowed after heavy rain.`,indoor:!1},{id:`garuda-wisnu-kencana`,name:`Garuda Wisnu Kencana Cultural Park`,localName:`Taman Budaya GWK`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`statue`,`culture`,`dance`,`sunset`],area:`Ungasan`,lat:-8.8104,lng:115.1675,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:8,rating:3,description:`A former limestone quarry crowned by a 121m statue of Vishnu riding the eagle Garuda, one of the world's tallest, with Balinese dance shows through the day.`,tip:`Come late afternoon for the dance performances and golden light on the statue.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Garuda Wisnu Kencana Cultural Park`},{id:`padang-padang-beach`,name:`Padang Padang Beach`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`beach`,`surf`,`swimming`,`photo-spot`],area:`Uluwatu`,lat:-8.8112,lng:115.1031,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:1,rating:3,description:`A small, picture-perfect cove reached through a narrow cleft in the cliffs, with calm swimming at low tide and a famous reef break for experts.`,tip:`Arrive early — the tiny beach is crowded by midday.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Padang Padang Beach`},{id:`rock-bar-bali`,name:`Rock Bar`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`bar`,`sunset`,`clifftop`,`cocktails`,`iconic`],area:`Jimbaran`,lat:-8.7862,lng:115.1355,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:4,description:`A bar perched on rocks 14m above the Indian Ocean at the AYANA resort, reached by an inclined lift and famed for its sunset views.`,tip:`Arrive by 4pm to beat the queue, and expect a minimum spend at sunset.`,indoor:!1},{id:`finns-beach-club`,name:`FINNS Beach Club`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`beach-club`,`sunset`,`pool`,`dj`],area:`Canggu`,lat:-8.6625,lng:115.1393,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:35,rating:3,description:`A huge, buzzing beach club on Berawa Beach with several pools, swim-up bars and DJs as the sun drops into the ocean.`,tip:`Book a daybed ahead at weekends; minimum spends apply.`,indoor:!1},{id:`yoga-barn`,name:`The Yoga Barn`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`yoga`,`wellness`,`sound-healing`,`classes`],area:`Ubud`,lat:-8.5164,lng:115.2652,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:3,description:`Ubud's best-known wellness hub, a riverside garden of open-air studios running drop-in yoga, meditation and sound-healing sessions all day.`,indoor:!1},{id:`gianyar-night-market`,name:`Gianyar Night Market`,localName:`Pasar Senggol Gianyar`,category:`food`,tags:[`night-market`,`street-food`,`babi-guling`,`local-favourite`,`budget`],area:`Gianyar`,lat:-8.539,lng:115.3255,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:5,rating:4,description:`A bustling evening food market in Gianyar town where locals feast on babi guling, sate and martabak at rock-bottom prices.`,indoor:!1},{id:`bali-safari-park`,name:`Bali Safari Park`,category:`family`,tags:[`wildlife`,`kids`,`safari`,`shows`],area:`Gianyar`,lat:-8.5806,lng:115.3526,durationHours:4,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:55,rating:3,description:`A large safari park where trams carry you past tigers, lions and Komodo dragons, with animal shows and a water-play zone for kids.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Bali Safari and Marine Park`},{id:`neka-art-museum`,name:`Neka Art Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`rainy-day`,`balinese`,`gardens`],area:`Ubud`,lat:-8.4951,lng:115.2504,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:6,rating:3,description:`A thoughtful survey of Balinese painting from classical Kamasan styles to works by expatriate artists such as Arie Smit, in pavilions just north of Ubud centre.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Neka Art Museum`},{id:`sanur-beach`,name:`Sanur Beach Promenade`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`beach`,`sunrise`,`cycling`,`free`,`kids`],area:`Sanur`,lat:-8.6766,lng:115.2634,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A calm, reef-sheltered beach with a 5km seaside path ideal for sunrise strolls and cycling past colourful jukung outrigger boats.`,tip:`Rent a bicycle and ride the path at dawn; fast boats to Nusa Penida leave from here.`,indoor:!1}],foods:[{name:`Suckling Pig`,localName:`Babi Guling`,description:`Spit-roasted pig stuffed with turmeric and spices, served with crackling, lawar and sambal over rice.`},{name:`Slow-Cooked Spiced Duck`,localName:`Bebek Betutu`,description:`Duck rubbed with a rich spice paste, wrapped in banana leaves and slow-cooked until falling apart.`},{name:`Minced Satay`,localName:`Sate Lilit`,description:`Spiced minced fish or chicken with coconut, wrapped around lemongrass stalks and grilled.`},{name:`Lawar`,description:`A traditional mix of chopped vegetables, grated coconut, minced meat and spices, often served at ceremonies.`},{name:`Nasi Campur Bali`,description:`Rice with a sampler of small portions: shredded chicken, sate lilit, vegetables, peanuts and sambal matah.`},{name:`Black Rice Pudding`,localName:`Bubur Injin`,description:`Sweet, nutty black glutinous rice porridge topped with coconut milk — a classic Balinese breakfast or dessert.`}]},{id:`jakarta`,name:`Jakarta`,lat:-6.2088,lng:106.8456,timezone:`Asia/Jakarta`,tagline:`Megacity of colonial relics, malls and Betawi street food`,description:`Indonesia's sprawling capital is chaotic but rewarding, with Dutch-era Kota Tua, grand national monuments, world-class malls and a buzzing food and nightlife scene. The MRT and Grab make it far easier to get around than its traffic reputation suggests.`,idealDays:[2,3],places:[{id:`national-monument`,name:`National Monument`,localName:`Monumen Nasional (Monas)`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`viewpoint`,`history`,`night-view`],area:`Merdeka Square`,lat:-6.1754,lng:106.8272,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:2,rating:4,description:`A 132m obelisk topped with a gold-leaf flame, rising from vast Merdeka Square, with a history diorama museum at its base.`,tip:`Get there early for the lift to the top deck (limited daily tickets); the monument is lit up beautifully after dark.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`National Monument (Indonesia)`},{id:`istiqlal-mosque`,name:`Istiqlal Mosque`,localName:`Masjid Istiqlal`,category:`culture`,tags:[`mosque`,`free`,`rainy-day`,`architecture`,`guided-tour`],area:`Merdeka Square`,lat:-6.1702,lng:106.831,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Southeast Asia's largest mosque, a vast modernist hall that holds over 100,000 worshippers.`,tip:`Visitors join a free guided tour from the visitor desk outside prayer times; modest dress required, robes provided.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Istiqlal Mosque`},{id:`jakarta-cathedral`,name:`Jakarta Cathedral`,localName:`Gereja Katedral Jakarta`,category:`culture`,tags:[`church`,`neo-gothic`,`free`,`rainy-day`],area:`Merdeka Square`,lat:-6.1693,lng:106.8331,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A neo-Gothic cathedral from 1901 facing Istiqlal Mosque across the street — a symbol of Indonesian religious tolerance.`,tip:`Visit the small museum upstairs; the "tunnel of friendship" connects the cathedral and mosque underground.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Jakarta Cathedral`},{id:`national-museum-indonesia`,name:`National Museum of Indonesia`,localName:`Museum Nasional (Museum Gajah)`,category:`museum`,tags:[`history`,`rainy-day`,`archaeology`,`ethnography`],area:`Merdeka Square`,lat:-6.1763,lng:106.8217,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:4,rating:4,description:`Known as the Elephant Museum for the bronze elephant out front, it holds superb Hindu-Buddhist statues, ethnographic treasures and royal gold.`,tip:`Closed on Mondays; book tickets online in advance since its 2024 reopening.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`National Museum of Indonesia`},{id:`fatahillah-square`,name:`Fatahillah Square & Jakarta History Museum`,localName:`Taman Fatahillah`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`colonial`,`history`,`old-town`,`bicycles`,`iconic`],area:`Kota Tua`,lat:-6.1352,lng:106.8133,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:1,rating:4,description:`The cobbled heart of Dutch Batavia, ringed by the 1710 city hall (now the Jakarta History Museum), the Wayang Museum and colourful hire bikes.`,tip:`Rent a vintage bicycle and floppy hat on the square for photos; museums close on Mondays.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Jakarta History Museum`},{id:`cafe-batavia`,name:`Café Batavia`,category:`food`,tags:[`colonial`,`restaurant`,`heritage`,`rainy-day`],area:`Kota Tua`,lat:-6.1348,lng:106.8129,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:3,description:`A grand two-storey colonial-era building on Fatahillah Square, with teak floors and walls lined with vintage photos.`,tip:`Ask for a window table upstairs overlooking the square.`,indoor:!0},{id:`sunda-kelapa`,name:`Sunda Kelapa Old Port`,localName:`Pelabuhan Sunda Kelapa`,category:`culture`,tags:[`harbour`,`schooners`,`photo-spot`,`history`],area:`Kota Tua`,lat:-6.1229,lng:106.81,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:1,rating:3,description:`Jakarta's original harbour, where rows of wooden Bugis pinisi schooners still load cargo by hand.`,tip:`Go early morning for the best light and activity; nearby Museum Bahari occupies old Dutch spice warehouses.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Sunda Kelapa`},{id:`petak-sembilan`,name:`Glodok Chinatown & Petak Sembilan`,localName:`Pecinan Glodok`,category:`food`,tags:[`chinatown`,`street-food`,`temple`,`market`],area:`Glodok`,lat:-6.1435,lng:106.813,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:6,rating:3,description:`Jakarta's Chinatown, a warren of wet markets and food alleys around the 17th-century Vihara Dharma Bhakti temple.`,tip:`Explore Gang Gloria alley for old-school snacks like kopi es Tak Kie and pork bakmi.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Glodok`},{id:`jalan-sabang`,name:`Jalan Sabang`,category:`food`,tags:[`street-food`,`satay`,`night-market`,`budget`],area:`Menteng`,lat:-6.1847,lng:106.8262,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:5,rating:3,description:`A central street that fills with food carts and kaki lima stalls after dark — satay, nasi goreng, martabak and soto.`,tip:`A good first stop for Jakarta street food, a short walk from Monas and the Thamrin hotels.`,indoor:!1},{id:`grand-indonesia`,name:`Grand Indonesia`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`mall`,`rainy-day`,`air-conditioned`,`food-court`],area:`Thamrin`,lat:-6.1951,lng:106.8209,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`One of Southeast Asia's largest malls, with hundreds of shops, a cinema and an excellent food court on Jalan Thamrin.`,tip:`Connected to Bundaran HI MRT station — the easiest way to beat traffic.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Grand Indonesia`},{id:`bundaran-hi`,name:`Hotel Indonesia Roundabout`,localName:`Bundaran HI`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`free`,`night-view`,`fountain`,`car-free-day`],area:`Thamrin`,lat:-6.1949,lng:106.823,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`The Welcome Monument fountain at the heart of Jakarta, surrounded by skyscrapers and lit up at night.`,tip:`On Sunday mornings (6–10am) Jalan Thamrin becomes Car Free Day, packed with joggers, cyclists and snack vendors.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Selamat Datang Monument`},{id:`skye-bar`,name:`SKYE`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`rooftop-bar`,`night-view`,`sunset`,`cocktails`],area:`Thamrin`,lat:-6.1965,lng:106.8226,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:4,description:`A 56th-floor rooftop bar and restaurant atop Menara BCA with a pool-side terrace and panoramic views over the city lights.`,tip:`Smart dress code; arrive around 5:30pm for sunset and a terrace seat.`,indoor:!1},{id:`blok-m`,name:`Blok M & Little Tokyo`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`bars`,`izakaya`,`street-food`,`nightlife`],area:`Blok M`,lat:-6.243,lng:106.7995,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:15,rating:3,description:`A revived South Jakarta hub of izakayas, craft-beer bars and food stalls around the Melawai "Little Tokyo" streets.`,tip:`Take the MRT to Blok M station and walk through the trendy Blok M Hub for street food first.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Blok M`},{id:`museum-macan`,name:`Museum MACAN`,category:`museum`,tags:[`contemporary-art`,`rainy-day`,`kids`,`air-conditioned`],area:`Kebon Jeruk`,lat:-6.1903,lng:106.7676,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:7,rating:4,description:`Indonesia's first international modern and contemporary art museum, with rotating blockbuster exhibitions and a dedicated children's art space.`,tip:`Book timed tickets online; closed Mondays.`,indoor:!0},{id:`taman-mini-indonesia-indah`,name:`Taman Mini Indonesia Indah`,category:`family`,tags:[`culture`,`kids`,`theme-park`,`architecture`],area:`Taman Mini`,lat:-6.3024,lng:106.8952,durationHours:4,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:3,rating:3,description:`A huge cultural park with traditional houses from every Indonesian province, museums and a cable car over a lake shaped like the archipelago.`,tip:`It is big and hot — rent a bicycle or use the shuttle buses between pavilions.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Taman Mini Indonesia Indah`},{id:`dunia-fantasi`,name:`Dunia Fantasi (Dufan)`,category:`family`,tags:[`theme-park`,`kids`,`rides`,`seaside`],area:`Ancol`,lat:-6.1253,lng:106.8333,durationHours:6,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:19,rating:3,description:`Jakarta's biggest amusement park within the seafront Ancol Dreamland complex, with roller coasters, water rides and shows.`,tip:`Weekdays are much quieter; an Ancol gate fee is charged separately from Dufan entry.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Dunia Fantasi`},{id:`ragunan-zoo`,name:`Ragunan Zoo`,localName:`Taman Margasatwa Ragunan`,category:`nature`,tags:[`zoo`,`kids`,`park`,`orangutans`,`budget`],area:`Ragunan`,lat:-6.3125,lng:106.8202,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:1,rating:3,description:`A leafy 140-hectare zoo, one of Jakarta's greenest spaces, home to Komodo dragons and orangutans in the Schmutzer Primate Centre.`,tip:`Closed Mondays; payment is cashless via a JakCard/e-money card bought at the gate.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Ragunan Zoo`},{id:`setu-babakan`,name:`Setu Babakan Betawi Cultural Village`,localName:`Perkampungan Budaya Betawi`,category:`culture`,tags:[`betawi`,`village`,`free`,`lake`,`food`],area:`Jagakarsa`,lat:-6.3412,lng:106.8236,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A lakeside village preserving the culture of Jakarta's native Betawi people, with traditional houses, a small museum and snack stalls.`,tip:`Weekends bring dance and martial-arts performances and the best choice of kerak telor stalls.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Setu Babakan`},{id:`wayang-museum`,name:`Wayang Museum`,localName:`Museum Wayang`,category:`museum`,tags:[`puppets`,`rainy-day`,`heritage`,`kids`],area:`Kota Tua`,lat:-6.1349,lng:106.8122,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:1,rating:3,description:`A museum on the site of an old Dutch church on Fatahillah Square, displaying hundreds of shadow and rod puppets from across Indonesia and beyond.`,tip:`Closed on Mondays; check for occasional weekend wayang performances.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Wayang Museum`},{id:`museum-bahari`,name:`Maritime Museum`,localName:`Museum Bahari`,category:`museum`,tags:[`maritime`,`history`,`warehouses`,`rainy-day`],area:`Kota Tua`,lat:-6.1268,lng:106.8087,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:1,rating:3,description:`Restored 17th-century Dutch East India Company spice warehouses filled with traditional boats and exhibits on the archipelago's seafaring past.`,tip:`Combine with the Sunda Kelapa schooners a short walk away.`,indoor:!0},{id:`bank-indonesia-museum`,name:`Bank Indonesia Museum`,localName:`Museum Bank Indonesia`,category:`museum`,tags:[`history`,`money`,`rainy-day`,`air-conditioned`,`architecture`],area:`Kota Tua`,lat:-6.1371,lng:106.8131,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:1,rating:3,description:`A grand neo-classical former bank with stained glass and slick air-conditioned galleries on Indonesia's economic history, from the spice trade to the rupiah.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Bank Indonesia Museum`},{id:`national-gallery-indonesia`,name:`National Gallery of Indonesia`,localName:`Galeri Nasional Indonesia`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`rainy-day`,`colonial`],area:`Merdeka Square`,lat:-6.1785,lng:106.8329,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A colonial-era building just east of Merdeka Square showing modern Indonesian art and changing contemporary exhibitions, usually free to enter.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`National Gallery of Indonesia`},{id:`lapangan-banteng`,name:`Lapangan Banteng`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`park`,`fountain`,`free`,`light-show`,`night-view`],area:`Pasar Baru`,lat:-6.1708,lng:106.8352,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A revamped colonial square dominated by the dramatic West Irian Liberation Monument, with a musical fountain show on weekend evenings.`,tip:`Pair it with Istiqlal Mosque and Jakarta Cathedral, a five-minute walk away.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Lapangan Banteng`},{id:`pasar-baru`,name:`Pasar Baru`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`market`,`textiles`,`heritage`,`bargaining`],area:`Pasar Baru`,lat:-6.1636,lng:106.834,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Jakarta's oldest shopping street, dating from 1820, a pedestrian arcade lined with tailors, fabric merchants and old Indian and Chinese shops.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Pasar Baru`},{id:`sarinah`,name:`Sarinah`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`crafts`,`batik`,`souvenirs`,`rainy-day`,`air-conditioned`],area:`Thamrin`,lat:-6.1874,lng:106.8236,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Indonesia's first department store, reborn in 2022 as a showcase for local design, batik, coffee and crafts from across the archipelago.`,indoor:!0},{id:`plaza-indonesia`,name:`Plaza Indonesia`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`mall`,`luxury`,`rainy-day`,`air-conditioned`,`dining`],area:`Thamrin`,lat:-6.1932,lng:106.8221,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`An upscale mall on the Bundaran HI roundabout with luxury labels and a busy dining scene, a short walk from Grand Indonesia.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Plaza Indonesia`},{id:`taman-suropati`,name:`Taman Suropati`,category:`nature`,tags:[`park`,`free`,`music`,`menteng`],area:`Menteng`,lat:-6.1993,lng:106.8325,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A shady colonial-era park in leafy Menteng, surrounded by grand Dutch villas, where amateur musicians gather to play on weekends.`,tip:`Walk on to the Jalan Surabaya flea market for antiques and old vinyl.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Taman Suropati`},{id:`pecenongan-food-street`,name:`Jalan Pecenongan Night Food Street`,category:`food`,tags:[`street-food`,`martabak`,`seafood`,`night-market`,`budget`],area:`Pecenongan`,lat:-6.1683,lng:106.8238,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:6,rating:3,description:`A long strip just north of Monas that comes alive at night with seafood tents and some of Jakarta's most famous martabak stalls.`,indoor:!1},{id:`henshin`,name:`Henshin`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`rooftop-bar`,`night-view`,`cocktails`,`sunset`],area:`Kuningan`,lat:-6.2265,lng:106.8296,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:4,description:`A Peruvian-Japanese restaurant and bar on the top floors of The Westin, one of the city's highest, with open-air terraces over the Jakarta skyline.`,tip:`Smart-casual dress code; book a terrace table for sunset.`,indoor:!1},{id:`kemang`,name:`Kemang`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`bars`,`cafes`,`live-music`,`expat`],area:`Kemang`,lat:-6.261,lng:106.8135,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:15,rating:3,description:`An expat-favourite South Jakarta neighbourhood packed with cafés, restaurants, live-music bars and design shops along Jalan Kemang Raya.`,indoor:!1},{id:`jakarta-aquarium`,name:`Jakarta Aquarium & Safari`,category:`family`,tags:[`aquarium`,`kids`,`rainy-day`,`air-conditioned`],area:`Grogol`,lat:-6.1749,lng:106.7907,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:15,rating:3,description:`A large indoor aquarium and mini safari inside the Neo Soho mall, with a mermaid show, touch pools and tropical animal encounters.`,indoor:!0},{id:`kidzania-jakarta`,name:`KidZania Jakarta`,category:`family`,tags:[`kids`,`role-play`,`rainy-day`,`air-conditioned`],area:`SCBD`,lat:-6.2245,lng:106.81,durationHours:4,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:3,description:`A child-sized city inside Pacific Place mall where kids role-play dozens of jobs, from pilot to firefighter, earning their own currency.`,indoor:!0},{id:`bogor-botanical-gardens`,name:`Bogor Botanical Gardens`,localName:`Kebun Raya Bogor`,category:`nature`,tags:[`gardens`,`day-trip`,`history`,`palace`],area:`Bogor`,lat:-6.5976,lng:106.7996,durationHours:5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:5,rating:4,description:`A vast botanical garden founded in 1817 beside the Bogor Presidential Palace, with towering trees, giant water lilies and orchid houses.`,tip:`Take the KRL commuter train from Jakarta (about 1.5 hours) and go on a weekday morning.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Bogor Botanical Gardens`},{id:`taman-safari`,name:`Taman Safari Indonesia`,category:`family`,tags:[`wildlife`,`safari`,`kids`,`day-trip`],area:`Puncak`,lat:-6.7176,lng:106.948,durationHours:6,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:4,description:`A drive-through safari park in the cool Puncak highlands where zebras, bears and giraffes approach your car, plus animal shows and a baby zoo.`,tip:`Leave Jakarta very early or go on a weekday — Puncak traffic is notorious.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Taman Safari`},{id:`thousand-islands`,name:`Thousand Islands Day Trip`,localName:`Kepulauan Seribu`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`island`,`snorkelling`,`day-trip`,`boat`,`beach`],area:`Thousand Islands`,lat:-5.745,lng:106.613,durationHours:9,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:35,rating:3,description:`A chain of small coral islands north of Jakarta Bay, reached by speedboat from Marina Ancol for snorkelling, white sand and clearer water.`,tip:`Book a resort day package from Marina Ancol, and avoid weekends and rough rainy-season seas.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Thousand Islands (Indonesia)`}],foods:[{name:`Betawi Beef Soup`,localName:`Soto Betawi`,description:`Beef and offal in a creamy coconut-milk and milk broth, served with emping crackers and lime.`},{name:`Kerak Telor`,description:`A crispy Betawi omelette of glutinous rice and duck egg, topped with fried shallots and toasted coconut.`},{name:`Nasi Uduk`,description:`Coconut-and-lemongrass rice served with fried chicken, tempeh, egg and sambal — a breakfast staple.`},{name:`Gado-Gado`,description:`Blanched vegetables, tofu, tempeh, egg and rice cakes smothered in peanut sauce with krupuk crackers.`},{name:`Ketoprak`,description:`Rice cake, tofu, vermicelli and bean sprouts in a garlicky peanut sauce, sold from street carts.`},{name:`Martabak Manis`,description:`A thick, fluffy sweet pancake folded with chocolate, cheese, peanuts or condensed milk — a late-night favourite.`}]},{id:`yogyakarta`,name:`Yogyakarta`,localName:`Jogja`,lat:-7.80139,lng:110.36444,timezone:`Asia/Jakarta`,tagline:`Sultan’s city of batik, gamelan and giant ancient temples`,description:`Java’s cultural heart is still ruled by a sultan, with a living palace, batik workshops and wayang puppet shows in the old town around the Kraton. Beyond the city lie Borobudur and Prambanan, the smoking cone of Merapi and the caves and beaches of the south coast, so plan early starts and a driver for day trips.`,idealDays:[3,6],places:[{id:`borobudur`,name:`Borobudur Temple`,localName:`Candi Borobudur`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`temple`,`buddhist`,`unesco`,`sunrise`],area:`Magelang`,lat:-7.608,lng:110.204,durationHours:4,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:28,rating:5,description:`The world’s largest Buddhist monument, a ninth-century stepped mandala of carved relief galleries rising to rows of stupas with views of the volcanoes.`,tip:`Climbing the structure needs a separate timed ticket with a daily quota, so book online days ahead; the yard ticket alone only lets you walk around the base.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Borobudur`},{id:`prambanan`,name:`Prambanan Temple`,localName:`Candi Prambanan`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`temple`,`hindu`,`unesco`,`photo-spot`],area:`Prambanan`,lat:-7.75222,lng:110.49167,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:5,description:`Soaring ninth-century Hindu towers dedicated to Shiva, Vishnu and Brahma, carved with the Ramayana and set in a park with several smaller temples.`,tip:`Late afternoon light on the spires is best; the ticket also covers the free shuttle to Sewu temple at the back of the park.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Prambanan`},{id:`ramayana-ballet`,name:`Ramayana Ballet at Prambanan`,localName:`Sendratari Ramayana`,category:`culture`,tags:[`dance`,`performance`,`gamelan`,`night`,`iconic`],area:`Prambanan`,lat:-7.752,lng:110.48856,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:18,rating:4,description:`A wordless dance drama of the Ramayana with a full gamelan orchestra, staged in the dry season on an open-air stage with the lit temples behind.`,tip:`Shows usually run Tuesday, Thursday and Saturday at 7:30pm; from November to April, or when it rains, they move to the indoor Trimurti stage.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Ramayana Ballet`},{id:`kraton`,name:`Kraton (Sultan’s Palace)`,localName:`Keraton Ngayogyakarta Hadiningrat`,category:`culture`,tags:[`palace`,`heritage`,`gamelan`,`iconic`],area:`Kraton`,lat:-7.80569,lng:110.36406,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:2,rating:5,description:`The still-inhabited palace of the sultans, a complex of airy Javanese pavilions with royal heirlooms, guards in traditional dress and daily gamelan or dance.`,tip:`Open mornings only and closed on Mondays; a short cultural performance is included most mornings around 10am.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Kraton Ngayogyakarta Hadiningrat`},{id:`taman-sari`,name:`Taman Sari Water Castle`,localName:`Taman Sari`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`palace`,`pools`,`heritage`,`photo-spot`],area:`Kraton`,lat:-7.81015,lng:110.35895,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:2,rating:4,description:`The 18th-century pleasure garden of the sultans, with turquoise bathing pools, an underground mosque and lanes of the surrounding kampung to wander.`,tip:`Do not miss the circular Sumur Gumuling mosque through the tunnels; politely decline unofficial guides who lead you to batik shops.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Taman Sari (Yogyakarta)`},{id:`malioboro`,name:`Malioboro Street`,localName:`Jalan Malioboro`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`street`,`shopping`,`batik`,`street-food`,`night`],area:`Malioboro`,lat:-7.79336,lng:110.36571,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Jogja’s main boulevard, lined with batik and souvenir stalls, buskers, horse carts and becak, and at its liveliest after dark.`,tip:`Bargain hard at the street stalls and agree becak fares before setting off; Mirota Batik near the south end has fixed prices.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Jalan Malioboro`},{id:`beringharjo-market`,name:`Beringharjo Market`,localName:`Pasar Beringharjo`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`market`,`batik`,`spices`,`local`,`rainy-day`],area:`Malioboro`,lat:-7.79886,lng:110.36542,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`The city’s historic central market, crammed with bolts of batik on the ground floor and herbs, spices and jamu ingredients upstairs.`,tip:`Go in the morning when it is cooler and busiest; the cheapest batik is in the west building.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Beringharjo`},{id:`ratu-boko`,name:`Ratu Boko`,localName:`Kraton Ratu Boko`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`ruins`,`hilltop`,`sunset`,`archaeology`],area:`Prambanan`,lat:-7.77,lng:110.48889,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:4,description:`Hilltop remains of an ancient palace complex with a grand stone gateway, bathing pools and sweeping views over the Prambanan plain to Merapi.`,tip:`Come for sunset and look for combination tickets with Prambanan, which save money over buying separately.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Ratu Boko`},{id:`merapi-lava-tour`,name:`Merapi Jeep Lava Tour`,localName:`Lava Tour Merapi`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`volcano`,`jeep`,`viewpoint`,`sunrise`],area:`Kaliurang`,lat:-7.58292,lng:110.4479,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:4,description:`Open-top jeep rides across the ash fields of Indonesia’s most active volcano, stopping at the Kaliadem bunker and villages buried in the 2010 eruption.`,tip:`Jeeps are priced per vehicle for up to four people; go at dawn for the clearest view of the summit before the clouds roll in.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Mount Merapi`},{id:`jomblang-cave`,name:`Jomblang Cave`,localName:`Goa Jomblang`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`cave`,`abseiling`,`light-rays`,`photo-spot`],area:`Gunungkidul`,lat:-8.02863,lng:110.63824,durationHours:5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:35,rating:4,description:`Be lowered by rope into a jungle-filled sinkhole, then walk through a cave passage to see the famous beam of sunlight falling into Grubug Cave.`,tip:`Only one descent session runs each morning with limited places, so book ahead; wear shoes you do not mind getting muddy.`,indoor:!1},{id:`pindul-cave`,name:`Pindul Cave Tubing`,localName:`Goa Pindul`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`cave`,`tubing`,`river`,`kids`],area:`Gunungkidul`,lat:-7.92943,lng:110.64035,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:5,rating:3,description:`Float on an inner tube through a limestone cave river past stalactites and bats, an easy and family-friendly taste of the karst hills.`,tip:`Pair it with Jomblang Cave on the same day; tubing after heavy rain may be suspended.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Pindul Cave`},{id:`parangtritis-beach`,name:`Parangtritis Beach`,localName:`Pantai Parangtritis`,category:`nature`,tags:[`beach`,`sunset`,`dunes`,`legend`],area:`Bantul`,lat:-8.01667,lng:110.35,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:1,rating:3,description:`A wide black-sand beach facing the Indian Ocean, tied to the legend of the sea goddess Nyi Roro Kidul, with horse carts, ATVs and sand dunes nearby.`,tip:`Do not swim: the currents are deadly. Come for sunset and a ride along the sand instead.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Parangtritis`},{id:`sewu-temple`,name:`Sewu Temple`,localName:`Candi Sewu`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`temple`,`buddhist`,`quiet`,`unesco`],area:`Prambanan`,lat:-7.74389,lng:110.4925,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A vast Buddhist temple complex of a main shrine ringed by more than 200 smaller ones, guarded by stone giants and far quieter than Prambanan.`,tip:`Entry is included in the Prambanan ticket; take the park shuttle or rent a bicycle to get there.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Sewu`},{id:`plaosan-temple`,name:`Plaosan Temple`,localName:`Candi Plaosan`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`temple`,`buddhist`,`quiet`,`sunrise`],area:`Prambanan`,lat:-7.74028,lng:110.50444,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:3,rating:3,description:`Twin Buddhist temples among rice fields with finely carved relief figures, often almost empty and lovely in early light.`,tip:`An easy add-on a short ride north-east of Prambanan.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Plaosan`},{id:`mendut-temple`,name:`Mendut Temple`,localName:`Candi Mendut`,category:`culture`,tags:[`temple`,`buddhist`,`monastery`,`sculpture`],area:`Magelang`,lat:-7.6048,lng:110.23008,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:1,rating:3,description:`A small ninth-century temple near Borobudur sheltering a serene three-metre stone Buddha, next to a working Buddhist monastery.`,tip:`Combine with tiny Pawon temple on the road to Borobudur; the three temples line up on one ancient axis.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Mendut`},{id:`punthuk-setumbu`,name:`Punthuk Setumbu Sunrise`,localName:`Bukit Punthuk Setumbu`,category:`nature`,tags:[`sunrise`,`viewpoint`,`volcano`,`mist`],area:`Magelang`,lat:-7.60741,lng:110.17784,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:3,rating:4,description:`A wooded hilltop viewpoint where Borobudur floats above the morning mist with Merapi and Merbabu behind it.`,tip:`Leave Jogja around 3:30am to be on the hill by 5am; mornings in the dry season give the best chance of mist without cloud.`,indoor:!1},{id:`ullen-sentalu`,name:`Ullen Sentalu Museum`,category:`museum`,tags:[`museum`,`javanese-royalty`,`batik`,`guided-tour`],area:`Kaliurang`,lat:-7.59797,lng:110.42317,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:6,rating:4,description:`A beautifully designed private museum in the cool Merapi foothills, telling the stories of Javanese royal women through portraits, letters and batik.`,tip:`Visits are by guided tour only and photography is not allowed inside; closed on Mondays.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Ullen Sentalu Museum`},{id:`sonobudoyo-museum`,name:`Sonobudoyo Museum`,localName:`Museum Sonobudoyo`,category:`museum`,tags:[`museum`,`wayang`,`puppets`,`rainy-day`,`night`],area:`Kraton`,lat:-7.80178,lng:110.364,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:2,rating:3,description:`Javanese culture museum on the north square with puppets, masks, keris daggers and textiles, and nightly shadow puppet performances.`,tip:`The evening wayang kulit show usually starts around 8pm; arrive in time to sit behind the screen as well as in front.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Sonobudoyo Museum`},{id:`fort-vredeburg`,name:`Fort Vredeburg Museum`,localName:`Benteng Vredeburg`,category:`museum`,tags:[`fort`,`history`,`colonial`,`rainy-day`],area:`Malioboro`,lat:-7.80037,lng:110.36638,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:1,rating:3,description:`A Dutch colonial fort facing the palace, now a museum of dioramas on Indonesia’s independence struggle.`,tip:`A cool break at the southern end of Malioboro; the ramparts are a good spot at dusk.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Fort Vredeburg Museum`},{id:`kotagede`,name:`Kotagede Old Town`,localName:`Kotagede`,category:`culture`,tags:[`old-town`,`silver`,`heritage`,`walking`],area:`Kotagede`,lat:-7.81786,lng:110.39541,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The 16th-century capital of the Mataram kingdom, with narrow walled lanes, a royal mosque and cemetery, and silversmith workshops.`,tip:`Many silver workshops let you watch filigree being made and run short jewellery-making classes.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Kotagede`},{id:`alun-alun-kidul`,name:`Alun-Alun Kidul`,localName:`Alkid`,category:`family`,tags:[`square`,`night`,`banyan-trees`,`light-bikes`,`local`],area:`Kraton`,lat:-7.81184,lng:110.3632,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:3,rating:3,description:`The palace’s southern square, where locals gather at night to pedal neon-lit carts, try to walk blindfolded between the twin banyan trees and snack at stalls.`,tip:`Agree the price of the light bike before you ride; weekends are the busiest and most fun.`,indoor:!1},{id:`tugu-monument`,name:`Tugu Monument`,localName:`Tugu Yogyakarta`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`monument`,`night`,`photo-spot`,`symbol`],area:`Tugu`,lat:-7.78292,lng:110.36709,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:2,description:`The white obelisk at the main crossroads, on the sacred axis linking Mount Merapi, the palace and the sea, and the city’s favourite selfie spot.`,tip:`Best combined with a late-night coffee at the angkringan stalls behind Tugu station.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Tugu Yogyakarta`},{id:`affandi-museum`,name:`Affandi Museum`,localName:`Museum Affandi`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`painting`,`gallery`,`rainy-day`],area:`Gondokusuman`,lat:-7.7827,lng:110.3963,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:5,rating:3,description:`The riverside home and galleries of Indonesia’s great expressionist painter, with his swirling canvases and the leaf-shaped roofs he designed.`,tip:`The ticket includes a drink at the small café in the garden.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Affandi Museum`},{id:`gembira-loka-zoo`,name:`Gembira Loka Zoo`,localName:`Kebun Binatang Gembira Loka`,category:`family`,tags:[`zoo`,`animals`,`kids`,`park`],area:`Umbulharjo`,lat:-7.80397,lng:110.39787,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:5,rating:2,description:`A large, shady city zoo with Komodo dragons, orangutans and Sumatran tigers, plus boat rides and play areas for children.`,tip:`Go early on weekdays before the heat and school groups arrive.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Gembira Loka Zoo`},{id:`ijo-temple`,name:`Ijo Temple`,localName:`Candi Ijo`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`temple`,`hindu`,`sunset`,`viewpoint`],area:`Prambanan`,lat:-7.78389,lng:110.51222,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:1,rating:3,description:`The highest temple site around Yogyakarta, a terraced Hindu complex on a hillside looking out over the plain to the airport and the sunset.`,tip:`Pair it with Tebing Breksi just below for a late-afternoon loop.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Ijo Temple`},{id:`tebing-breksi`,name:`Tebing Breksi`,category:`nature`,tags:[`quarry`,`carvings`,`sunset`,`viewpoint`,`photo-spot`],area:`Prambanan`,lat:-7.78143,lng:110.50498,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:1,rating:3,description:`A former limestone quarry turned park, with giant carvings cut into the cliff, an amphitheatre and broad sunset views towards Merapi.`,tip:`Weekend evenings get crowded with locals; jeep tours from here also visit nearby temples.`,indoor:!1},{id:`kalibiru`,name:`Kalibiru Viewpoint`,localName:`Wisata Alam Kalibiru`,category:`nature`,tags:[`viewpoint`,`forest`,`reservoir`,`photo-spot`],area:`Kulon Progo`,lat:-7.80825,lng:110.12942,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:2,rating:2,description:`A community-run forest in the Menoreh hills with treetop platforms overlooking the Sermo reservoir, plus flying-fox lines.`,tip:`Each treetop platform photo session costs extra; come early before haze softens the view.`,indoor:!1},{id:`mangunan-pine-forest`,name:`Mangunan Pine Forest`,localName:`Hutan Pinus Mangunan`,category:`nature`,tags:[`forest`,`pine`,`walking`,`mist`],area:`Dlingo`,lat:-7.92287,lng:110.43411,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:1,rating:3,description:`Tall rows of pines on the hills south of the city, cool and misty in the morning, with wooden walkways and nearby valley viewpoints.`,tip:`Combine with the Mangunan fruit garden viewpoint and Sate Klatak in Bantul on the way back.`,indoor:!1},{id:`kaliurang`,name:`Kaliurang Hill Resort`,localName:`Kaliurang`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`hill-station`,`cool-air`,`park`,`volcano`],area:`Kaliurang`,lat:-7.6,lng:110.4167,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:1,rating:2,description:`A cool, leafy hill town on Merapi’s southern slope where Jogja families escape the heat, with a forest park, waterfalls and roasted corn stalls.`,tip:`Stop at Ullen Sentalu Museum here and Kopi Klotok on the drive down.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Kaliurang`},{id:`prawirotaman`,name:`Prawirotaman Street`,localName:`Jalan Prawirotaman`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`bars`,`cafes`,`live-music`,`night`,`backpacker`],area:`Prawirotaman`,lat:-7.81915,lng:110.37064,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:8,rating:3,description:`The traveller quarter south of the palace, a strip of cafés, small bars, galleries and guesthouses that stays lively into the night.`,tip:`Most bars serve beer, which is harder to find in other parts of the city.`,indoor:!1},{id:`angkringan-tugu`,name:`Angkringan Lik Man`,localName:`Kopi Joss Lik Man`,category:`food`,tags:[`street-food`,`kopi-joss`,`night`,`local`],area:`Tugu`,lat:-7.7883,lng:110.3654,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:2,rating:3,description:`The best known of the angkringan stalls behind Tugu station, serving kopi joss (coffee with a glowing charcoal ember) to people sitting on mats on the pavement.`,tip:`Busiest from 9pm to past midnight; grab a few sate and nasi kucing parcels and pay at the cart.`,indoor:!1},{id:`kauman-great-mosque`,name:`Great Mosque of Kauman`,localName:`Masjid Gedhe Kauman`,category:`culture`,tags:[`mosque`,`heritage`,`architecture`,`royal`],area:`Kraton`,lat:-7.80395,lng:110.36256,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:2,description:`The sultanate’s royal mosque on the north square, built in 1773 with a tiered Javanese roof and a wide pillared veranda.`,tip:`Dress modestly and avoid prayer times; the Kauman lanes behind it are the birthplace of Muhammadiyah.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Kauman Great Mosque`},{id:`kasongan`,name:`Kasongan Pottery Village`,localName:`Desa Wisata Kasongan`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`pottery`,`crafts`,`village`,`workshop`],area:`Bantul`,lat:-7.8458,lng:110.342,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:2,description:`A village of terracotta workshops and showrooms selling everything from giant vases to small figurines, a short drive south-west of the city.`,tip:`Several workshops let you try the potter’s wheel for a small fee; shops can arrange shipping for large pieces.`,indoor:!1},{id:`dieng-plateau`,name:`Dieng Plateau Day Trip`,localName:`Dataran Tinggi Dieng`,category:`nature`,tags:[`volcanic`,`temples`,`crater`,`lake`,`day-trip`],area:`Wonosobo`,lat:-7.2,lng:109.9,durationHours:10,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:40,rating:3,description:`A high volcanic plateau with some of Java’s oldest Hindu temples, steaming craters and the coloured Telaga Warna lake, about four hours’ drive away.`,tip:`Hire a driver for a very long day, or stay a night for the sunrise from Sikunir hill; bring a jacket, as it is cold at 2,000 metres.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Dieng Plateau`}],foods:[{name:`Gudeg`,description:`Young jackfruit slow-cooked for hours in coconut milk and palm sugar, served with rice, chicken, egg and spicy beef-skin stew.`},{name:`Goat Satay on Bicycle Spokes`,localName:`Sate Klatak`,description:`Goat or lamb seasoned only with salt and grilled on iron bicycle spokes over charcoal, with a light curry broth on the side.`},{name:`Javanese Charcoal Noodles`,localName:`Bakmi Jawa`,description:`Noodles fried or in soup with chicken, egg and greens, cooked to order over a charcoal brazier.`},{name:`Cat Rice`,localName:`Nasi Kucing`,description:`Tiny banana-leaf parcels of rice with a dab of sambal or fish, eaten with skewers at night-time angkringan carts.`},{name:`Bakpia`,localName:`Bakpia Pathok`,description:`Small flaky pastries filled with sweet mung bean paste, the classic Jogja souvenir, best bought warm.`},{name:`Charcoal Coffee`,localName:`Kopi Joss`,description:`Sweet black coffee with a red-hot piece of charcoal dropped in, a late-night speciality of the stalls near Tugu station.`}]}]};export{e as indonesia};